00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.750 align:start position:0%
 
we're back with more things you didn't  know about breath of the wild this time  we're jumping a little more into secrets  about how damage works in the game that  you might not have known about so if you  enjoy our series here on gamespot hit  that like button we appreciate it  alrighty here we go  the famed lord of the mountain as many  people know is in honor of the late  satoru iwata and he only shows up on  certain faces of the moon specifically  starting on a phase called the waxing  crescent this isn't a coincidence though  as this is the moon phase that iwata was  born in the waxing crescent phase  people also pointed out in the last  video that quince's dog sari is a  nickname short for satori since he was  found on satori mountain socie is  inadvertently named after satoru iwata  now we gotta keep this precious pup safe  stall enemies will never fall for food  bait because well they obviously have no  stomachs  except for stall horses they can't help  themselves if a horsey treat presents  itself where does it go though  most players think that master sword  beams take durability well they're half  right they do when it's not powered up  when you get the fully upgraded master  sword the beams will take zero  durability otherwise they will consume  durability as normal so yes get an  upgraded asap so you can use those sword  beams without the durability hassle also  the master swords beam has different  properties against trees at close or  farther ranges when it's up close it can  cut down trees easily but loses this  ability after a certain distance did you  know that rock octorocks can throw  boomerangs unfortunately they can't  catch them again  it's a tiny detail but when you jump  attack with a spear off of a mount it's  actually a special animation that is  different from your normal jumping spear  attack  as a guy who's been riding for 11 years  that's me i've got some personal insight  to the master cycle the master cycle was  inspired by agl numa's personal love for  motorcycles but the final design for the  game had to be designed off of a dirt  bike for off-roading as a sport bike  wouldn't quite work in the rough terrain  of breath of the wild the developers  even purchased a dirt bike to ride it  themselves to understand its physics  drifting on it is pretty dramatic  compared to actual dirt bike cornering  but it does have the detail of having  the inside foot off the peg which is  standard practice while cornering on a  dirt bike and link does have decent head  placement while turning as you always  want to look ahead of the turn where you  want to go never in front of your tire  one detail they did omit though is the  master cycle has no gears as you'll  never hear the bike shift out of first  gear  well it is a magical bike after all a  concept idea for the master cycle was to  have it appear from a round device  resembling an ancient core after being  tossed on the floor likely for being a  nuisance to re-summon over and over this  idea was scrapped this gives me some  serious pokemon vibes though  while there have been some decent ways  to sneak into gerudo town without  changing outfits the newer method  involves the active aero smuggling trick  and the new campfire glitch  this lets you walk around scot-free  without getting caught well for at least  a little while  did you know that bouncing an object off  a wall as you throw them makes them go  farther  it can be pretty nifty to get some extra  reach for the jump on the enemy or  completing some puzzles  you can cancel out a wind cleavers air  slash with a lightning rod ball  [Applause]  a recent glitch found allows link to  carry any ingredient around as a  physical liftable object by using the  camera rune then holding an item quickly  dropping it then holding a different  item the dropped item is suspended in  mid-air now you can send shooting stars  back to where they came from  spicy peppers and sunshines create  updrafts when lit but there's a neat  trick involving letting them fall to  make a super updraft  by igniting them midair and letting them  fall stasising the ingredients will make  one super updraft  when you find a korok diving hole no  need to find a specific place to jump  off just bomb yourself and ragdoll into  the hole  [Music]  have you ever wondered what heart  containers are made of well you can  guess based off the sound they make when  you shield surf off of them  they sound pretty metallic to me  did you know that you can parry  backwards  the parry is accurate to the hitbox of  the shield itself not to link so if you  move over just a bit as an attack is  striking you it will miss link and hit  the shield instead now that's taking out  a guardian with style  [Music]  headshots are a great way to take down  enemies and have some hidden multipliers  such as the 10 times multiplier against  enemies on archer towers  but have you ever wondered why  headshotting wildlife always kills  instantly even with the wimpy bow  well that's because the multiplier is  actually times ten  thousand yup you heard me right so even  the weakest bow in the game does a  whopping 40 000 damage with a headshot  so if you ever want to feel good about  yourself use an ancient bow with ancient  armor and a triple attack buff head  shotting an animal will then do 1  million 180 000 damage you'll just never  actually see it now that's a lot of  damage it's fairly well known that most  mining weapons such as iron sledge  hammers and stone crushing weapons have  a bonus multiplier against taluses well  just be careful because nintendo just  straight up forgot to add this  multiplier to the luminous tiles  specifically they completely ignore  mining weapon multipliers so you're  better off with just using the best  weapon you got  did you know that nintendo planned to  have arrow crafting recipes in the game  they originally had these recipes set to  combine normal arrows with precious gems  to get different elements such as with  topaz to make shock arrows rubies to  make fire arrows and sapphires to make  ice arrows cast as most players know  travels about hyrule with his signature  instrument but this instrument isn't an  accordion it's called abandoning while  it's in the same instrument family its  key difference is its use of singular  buttons for notes instead of an  accordion's keys  the gates you walk through up the stairs  in reno village denote which floor  you're on by the number of feathers on  its wings  [Music]  link has multiple small animations for  opening chests such as standing in the  front for opening it normally crouching  in front of it to open it sneakily  standing on its size to kick it  crouching on the side to punch it  and kicking it with no pants on does a  number on his toes  [Music]  sometimes funny things are hidden in  plain sight if you talk to the npc  saguessa during the afternoon and say i  know about elixirs she'll comment about  how creeped out she is by how many twins  there are at this table  wait a second huh now that you mention  it that is weird  [Music]  and that's it what was your favorite  thing you learned this time let us know  in the comments below and if you  continue to enjoy new breath of the wild  videos we have a playlist with tons of  stuff we still make to this day for  everything else gaming keep it here on  gamespot  you

